WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.033
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.601
Welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:05.667
You're here!
You made it.

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:10.434
Well, guys, last night,
New York Yankees superstar

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:14.300
Aaron Judge made baseball
history and hit number 62.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:19.234
That's right.
Judge hit his 62nd home run

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:20.801
of the season
to break Roger Maris's

00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:22.334
American League record.

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:23.667
Of course,
right after it happened,

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.000
responses started pouring in.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.200
Everyone was tweeting about it.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.400
Even President Biden
congratulated him.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.767
This is real.
Biden tweeted...

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.801
That's nice.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:38.634
And Biden
sent another that said...

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:44.200
That was nice.
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.701
-Then Biden said...

00:00:47.534 --> 00:00:49.367
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.634
-That's really too much
information, almost.

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:52.834
And then Biden said...

00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:57.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:59.567
-Wow!
-Invented baseball.

00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:01.734
-He was there!
-He loves baseball.

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wow!

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.601
But listen to this.
The home-run ball itself

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:08.133
is thought to be worth
at least $2 million.

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:09.267
-Ooh.

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:11.334
And it was caught
by an investment banker.

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:14.601
-Ugh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:17.267
Huge moment for the Yankees
and an investment banker.

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:19.067
What a night
for the underdogs, you know?

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:20.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:21.801
Every fan of that game
last night

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:23.434
wanted to catch Judge's
home-run ball.

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:25.400
I think one guy
wanted it a bit too much.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.701
Watch this.
This is real.

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:29.634
-Go, go!
Soaring into history!

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:30.901
-Oh!
[ Cymbals crash ]

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:31.934
Oh!

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.434
-Well, that's one way
to beat traffic.

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:34.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.467
"I'm outta here."
Yeah.

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:36.968
Turns out the guy is okay.

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:39.133
He was actually caught
by an investment banker.

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:40.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:43.667
He's currently worth $2 million.

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:46.400
Switching gears, today, in the
aftermath of Hurricane Ian,

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.100
President Biden
travelled to Florida

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.133
and met with
Governor Ron DeSantis,

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:53.868
even though DeSantis has been
highly critical of Biden.

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:55.701
It's like that special episode
of a Disney sitcom

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:57.067
where the school bully realizes

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:58.400
he needs help
with his math homework.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.701
He's like, "Sorry
I called you those names."

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:03.567
But DeSantis
was actually nice to Biden.

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:04.634
He actually even offered him

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:06.200
a free flight
to Martha's Vineyard.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.067
I thought that was --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:12.434
Generous.

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:14.501
Well, I heard that former
President Trump has asked

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.601
the Supreme Court
to overturn a ruling

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:18.434
that allows
the Justice Department to review

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:20.467
roughly 100 classified documents

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:22.367
that were seized
from Mar-A-Lago.

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:24.400
Trump said, "It's my
Constitutional right.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.567
And I would know
'cause the original Constitution

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:28.434
is hanging in my bathroom
at Mar-A-Lago."

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:32.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:33.767
"I should know."

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:36.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:38.000
Speaking of Trump,
less than 24 hours

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.234
after announcing a defamation
lawsuit against CNN,

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:42.767
he sent out
a fundraising e-mail,

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:46.434
asking supporters to donate
$5 or more to his cause.

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:47.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.000
You know these are strange times

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.067
when you're the one sending
grandpa 5 bucks.

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:53.367
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.367 --> 00:02:55.167
Well, get this --
in Maggie Haberman's

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:58.100
new 608-page book
about the former president,

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.868
she wrote that, one time,
on a plane,

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:02.200
Trump made it a point
to loudly complain

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.767
after Rudy Giuliani
used the bathroom.

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:06.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.133 --> 00:03:09.000
Maggie, if you're watching,
I think a 607-page book

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.767
that left this story out
would have been just fine.

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:13.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:14.167
Apparently,
Trump yelled at Rudy,

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:15.400
he's like, "Have some respect.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.300
The Declaration of Independence
is in there."

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:21.367
Well, in a new interview,
Dr. Fauci said

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:24.000
at the start of the pandemic,
he should have been more careful

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.267
with his messaging on COVID.

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:28.067
Fauci was like, "In retrospect,
we shouldn't have ended

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:30.300
every CDC statement
with a question mark."

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:32.834
But Fauci also said...

00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:41.968
Or as Fox News reported it...

00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:48.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:49.567
That's not what he --

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:52.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:54.400
Well, people
are talking about this.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.367
In the new animated
"Scooby Doo" movie,

00:03:56.367 --> 00:03:59.033
Velma comes out as a lesbian.

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:02.334
Even more shocking,
Fred comes out as straight.

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:04.601
-Oy!
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:06.667
Whoa!

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.701
Whoa!
Zoinks!

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:09.868
Ruh-roh!

00:04:09.868 --> 00:04:13.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.334
-Some TV news.
"Frasier" is coming back

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:17.667
in a sequel series,
where he'll have all-new friends

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.601
and live in an all-new city.

00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:21.200
Yeah, on "Cheers,"
he was in Boston.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.400
Then he moved to Seattle.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.667
Now he's moving again.

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:25.200
I don't think Frasier's
a psychiatrist.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.434
I think he's a serial killer.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:28.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:29.634
Now, get this, everyone.
I saw that the producer

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:31.434
of James Bond
said that the next Bond

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:34.167
should be an actor in their 30s.

00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:36.200
Which means that Bond's
catchphrase is gonna sound

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.667
a little different.
Here are some options.

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:41.234
I'll give you an example.
Here we go.

00:04:41.234 --> 00:04:43.067
♪♪

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:49.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.400
♪♪

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:53.067
Sorry.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:54.567
♪♪

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:59.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:00.734
♪♪

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:05.234
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:06.834
♪♪

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:10.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.434
Listen, these are options.
That's just what --

00:05:12.434 --> 00:05:14.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.567
That's just what he might do.
-He might do that.

00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:17.968
-He's in his 30s.
Who knows?

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:20.734
He might do that.
He likes the kitchen backsplash.

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:23.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:24.133
You guys see this?

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:25.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.834 --> 00:05:27.701
That's what he enjoys, yeah.

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:29.367
"Thank you! I appreciate it.
I got it at Anthropologie,"

00:05:29.367 --> 00:05:31.601
yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:34.267
Did you guys see this?
A painting of a woman from 1860

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:36.534
is going viral because people
think she's walking

00:05:36.534 --> 00:05:37.868
while texting on an iPhone.

00:05:37.868 --> 00:05:39.567
Take a look at this.

00:05:39.567 --> 00:05:42.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:44.701
The name of the painting is
"Getting a DM from Adam Levine."

00:05:44.701 --> 00:05:46.133
-Whoa!
[ Cheers and laughter ]

00:05:46.133 --> 00:05:48.901
-That's the part I thought --
that's the part I thought was --

00:05:48.901 --> 00:05:52.400
that was, like, prescient.
-Maroon.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:55.434
-Yeah.
And, finally, a town in Canada

00:05:55.434 --> 00:05:58.868
just erected a roadside statue
of a giant Cheeto.

00:05:58.868 --> 00:06:03.868
Check it out.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.868 --> 00:06:06.100
Looks like they could've
erected it a little bit more.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:07.200
I'm just saying.
-Ayy!

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.100
Can we see that again?

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.767
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:06:11.767 --> 00:06:14.267
The name of that statue is
"Donald Trump at the Urinal."

00:06:14.267 --> 00:06:16.200
Hey, everyone,
we have a great show!

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

